# Cloudflare Pages Cache-Control rules
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# Rule of thumb:
#   - Anything in /assets/* is fingerprinted by Vite (e.g. index-DNAEeK1e.js),
#     so the URL changes on every deploy. Safe to cache forever.
#   - index.html / HTML routes must NOT be cached hard, otherwise users keep
#     loading stale asset manifests and the whole SPA breaks after a deploy.
#   - Top-level static files (favicon, og-image, sitemap, robots) sit at
#     stable URLs and update occasionally — a short-to-medium TTL is fine.
#
# Cloudflare Pages applies every matching rule; when the same header is set
# by more than one rule the LAST match wins. More specific rules therefore
# go BELOW the catch-all /* rule so they can override it.

# Catch-all — applies to every path unless overridden below.
# HTML routes land here (every SPA URL rewrites to /index.html via _redirects),
# so the default is "revalidate on every request" which is what the SPA shell
# needs to avoid serving a stale asset manifest after a deploy.
/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# Hashed JS/CSS/fonts/images emitted by Vite — cache forever, immutable.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Favicon, logo, icon sprite, OG image — refresh roughly daily.
/favicon.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/logo.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/icons.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/og-image.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

# Crawler-facing files — keep the TTL short so Google and Bing pick up new
# journal posts / station pages without a multi-hour cache delay.
/sitemap.xml
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

/robots.txt
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

/ads.txt
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
